                                                "sense_id": "220ae148-25bb-3d27-ab52-15aded58cccd",
                                                "text": "The first known way past the brick wall of Level 29 was a technique that became known as hypertapping. By using a special grip that lets you vibrate a finger over the D-pad directions at least 10 times a second, you can effectively skip the \"delayed autoshift\" (DAS) that limits how fast pieces can move laterally when the D-pad is held down."
                                            }
